1
00:06:50,526 --> 00:06:56,526
Adventure is reborn.

2
00:13:41,052 --> 00:13:47,052
The Mummy Returns is a adventure, action, fantasy
film directed by Stephen Sommers.

3
00:20:31,578 --> 00:20:37,578
Rick and Evelyn O’Connell, along with their 8-year-old son Alex, discover the key to
the legendary Scorpion King’s might: the fabled Bracelet of Anubis.

4
00:27:22,105 --> 00:27:28,105
Unfortunately, a newly resurrected Imhotep has designs on the bracelet as well, and isn’t above
kidnapping its new bearer, Alex, to gain control of Anubis’s otherworldly army.

5
00:34:12,631 --> 00:34:18,631
Rick O'Connell, played by Brendan Fraser.

6
00:41:03,157 --> 00:41:09,157
Evelyn O'Connell / Nefertiri, played by Rachel Weisz.

7
00:47:53,684 --> 00:47:59,684
Jonathan Carnahan, played by John Hannah.

8
00:54:44,210 --> 00:54:50,210
Ardeth Bay, played by Oded Fehr.

9
01:01:34,736 --> 01:01:40,736
Imhotep, played by Arnold Vosloo.

10
01:08:25,263 --> 01:08:31,263
Meela / Anck-Su-Namun, played by Patricia Velásquez.

11
01:15:15,789 --> 01:15:21,789
The Mummy Returns is a 2001 American fantasy action-adventure
film written and directed by Stephen Sommers.

12
01:22:06,315 --> 01:22:12,315
It is the sequel to the 1999 film The Mummy, and
the second in The Mummy film series.

13
01:28:56,842 --> 01:29:02,842
Brendan Fraser, Rachel Weisz, John Hannah, Arnold Vosloo, Oded Fehr, and Patricia Velásquez reprise their roles from the previous
film, with Dwayne Johnson (credited under his ring name "The Rock") joining the cast in his film acting debut.

14
01:35:47,368 --> 01:35:53,368
The film was released on May 4, 2001, by Universal Pictures.

15
01:42:37,894 --> 01:42:43,894
Like its predecessor, The Mummy Returns was a commercial success, grossing $435 million worldwide,
becoming the seventh-highest-grossing film of 2001 and the highest-grossing film of the series.

16
01:49:28,421 --> 01:49:34,421
The film received mixed reviews from critics.

17
01:56:18,947 --> 01:56:24,947
It was followed by a 2002 prequel film, The Scorpion King and a
2008 sequel, The Mummy: Tomb of the Dragon Emperor.

18
02:03:09,473 --> 02:03:15,473
The film explores themes of egypt, pyramid, son, mummy, nile.
